Z||000000||JohnnyK||08-08-2000||02:56 PM||||I want to get this radio back in (because it is backlit red, and mine isn't. UNless you know an easy way to change that?) But the buttons on the left (Volume, tuner, etc) have a mind of their own. It's not due to cleaning because there is some very wierd things going on. Usually, none of them will work, and then the volume button will control am/fm, and stuff like that. Anyone had this problem before?||||reg||1
Z||000001||vinnywolfe||08-08-2000||03:45 PM||||i had a radio just like that that was in a totalled out 85 gt that i bought.  i ended up going to a local car audio store that specialized in stock systems i had to buy the little rectangle shaped thing that contained all of the controls that you are talking about (volume, tuning, bal.).  it is on the left hand side of the radio.  anyway, the bad news is that the part cost $50.  but it fixed the problem and that is a small price to pay for such a nice stereo.<BR>i still say that delco makes the best stock sound system.  bar none.<P>hope this helped,<BR>vinny<BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||08-08-2000||05:11 PM||||I had the same probem on my previous 85 GT. the buttons are a carbon coated bubble. Through time and heat, they will go bad. Replace the control pad and it'll work properly again.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||wkayl||08-08-2000||08:28 PM||||vinnywolfe<BR>Can you let us know the name of the place where you got the part to fix your radio.  I took mine to the Pontiac dearler and they said it would be $350.00 to send it in to be repaired, including going over the tape deck.  Mine also had display problems (locking up or not coming on at all)||||reg||1
Z||000004||rockcrawl||08-08-2000||08:35 PM||||Hi,<BR> I called a local shop here in PA and the guy gave me a price of $38. for the button assy. He said he also has three of the Delco pushbutton radios on the shelf, if anyone is interested, let me know and I'll get prices on them. They will be totally reconditioned of course.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
